"""Direct loss (DL) per declared bushfire event × council, from public sources (collected 2026-09-27).

The unit is the 218 declared-event × council rows of out/key_event_council.csv (agrn, region_id = ABS LGA 2021
code). Output: one row per (agrn, region_id, metric, source), in data/enrich/dl_council.parquet and .csv.

Metrics: homes_destroyed, homes_damaged, facilities_destroyed / _damaged (non-residential buildings),
outbuildings_destroyed / _damaged, properties_destroyed / _damaged (the source says "properties", not homes),
fencing_km, livestock_lost, deaths, injuries.

Rules:
- Every value is hard-coded below with its source title, URL, page/section and a verbatim quote (<= 25 words) that
  contains the number (digits or words; a single named death may be counted from "died"/"took the life"). Every quote
  was checked word for word against the source text on 2026-09-27 (`quote_check` says how); `archive_url` is the
  Wayback copy read where the official site refuses scripted access. The build re-checks the number, the quote length and that
  (agrn, region_id) is one of the 218 rows, and fails otherwise.
- Hedged figures ("more than 300", "at least", "around") keep the number with hedged=True.
- Blank = unknown. 0 only where the source says none; mid-event "no reported losses" zeros say so in `note`.
- Sources that disagree each keep their own row. Nothing is summed, split or estimated.
- scope: "council_total" = the source's figure for all of the event's losses in that council;
  "fire_in_council" = one named fire inside the council (a lower bound when other fires also burned there);
  "statewide_zero" = the source reports zero for the whole state and season (so zero in every council).
- preferred: one value per (agrn, region_id, metric), chosen in this order: scope council_total > statewide_zero >
  fire_in_council, then not interim/superseded (per `note`), official > other > news, latest as_of_date, unhedged. Use it for a single figure per row.
- 2019-20 season-wide council figures sit on AGRN 871 (statewide declaration). AGRN 880 (North Coast, from 18 July
  2019) overlaps it in seven councils; a figure is put on 880 only where the source ties it to that declaration's fires.

Run: cd fire_event_dataset && ../.venv/bin/python -m src.dl_council
"""
